    "created_at": "2018-02-19T08:24:33Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-02-19T08:24:33Z",
    "body": "@GloverDonovan the behavior follows from the OverrideBuiltins declaration on HTMLFormElement coupled with that interface defining a getter.\r\n\r\nA note is probably sufficient for this. I don't think it needs to be `class=\"warning\"`. However, given that you probably want to explain it, you might want to use `<div>` with multiple paragraphs in it and an example.",
